#define HELP_GETTING_STARTED \
"wifisting GUI is a native GTK4 front-end for a collection of wireless\n" \
"security research scripts. Every module is a shell script under\n" \
"~/wifisting/modules/ that the GUI runs as a subprocess and renders\n" \
"as a structured panel.\n" \
"\n" \
"First-time setup\n" \
"  1. Dependency Manager  →  Install Missing\n" \
"     Installs the Debian packages the toolkit needs. Uses pkexec,\n" \
"     so you'll get one polkit password prompt.\n" \
"\n" \
"  2. Interface Manager   →  Kill Conflicts  →  Enable Monitor\n" \
"     Stops NetworkManager and wpa_supplicant, then puts the adapter\n" \
"     into monitor mode.\n" \
"\n" \
"  3. Wi-Fi Recon         →  Scan  →  Start  (Stop when ready)\n" \
"     Airodump-ng discovers nearby APs and clients. Counts appear in\n" \
"     the tab label while it runs.\n" \
"\n" \
"  4. Wi-Fi Recon         →  Targets  →  double-click a target\n" \
"     Selection propagates to the right-side target panel and to\n" \
"     every module that consumes a target.\n" \
"\n" \
"  5. From there, open WPA/2 Attack, Evil Twin, WPS, KRACK, or\n" \
"     PMKID. All of them pick up the target automatically.\n" \
"\n" \
"The header shows IFACE / MODE / MAC. A red value means the interface\n" \
"isn't in the state the tool expects. Amber is normal.\n"

#define HELP_KEYBOARD \
"Ctrl+P      Command palette. Search modules, run actions, kill\n" \
"            processes, copy loot paths.\n" \
"\n" \
"Ctrl+T      Open the Raw Terminal (VTE shell in the project dir).\n" \
"\n" \
