#define HELP_SAFETY \
"Authorized testing only.\n" \
"\n" \
"Active modules transmit real 802.11 frames. They are detectable from\n" \
"the air and can disrupt neighboring networks:\n" \
"\n" \
"  Deauth attacks       Disconnect legitimate clients.\n" \
"  Handshake capture    Passive sniff + deauth bursts.\n" \
"  Evil Twin            Impersonates an AP with a captive portal.\n" \
"  Karma                Answers every probe request.\n" \
"  Beacon Flood         Fills the air with thousands of fake SSIDs.\n" \
"  WPS / Pixie Dust     Actively attacks WPS-enabled APs.\n" \
"  PMKID                Sends association requests to the target.\n" \
"\n" \
"Use only against networks you own, lab or CTF environments, or\n" \
"engagements you have written authorization for.\n" \
"\n" \
"Hardware notes\n" \
"  Intel iwlwifi chipsets (9560, 9260, AX200, AX210) do not support\n" \
"  monitor mode or injection reliably. The kernel firmware silently\n" \
"  drops the interface back to managed mode at random intervals.\n" \
"\n" \
"  For reliable operation use a USB adapter with a proper chipset:\n" \
"    Atheros AR9271       ~$10     2.4 GHz    gold standard\n" \
"    Ralink RT3070/5370   ~$10-15  2.4 GHz    well supported\n" \
"    MediaTek MT7612U     ~$25     dual-band  modern\n" \
"    Alfa AWUS036ACH      ~$50     dual-band  high power\n" \
"\n" \
"  Bluetooth attacks need an nRF52840 dongle or an Ubertooth One.\n"

